#!/bin/bash
# land-letter-page.sh — the astrology letter is printed on paper. White ground,
# black editorial type, a serif title, one narrow column. The sidebar is not
# touched, by instruction.
#
# FRONTEND ONLY (together-city-react). Push, and Vercel ships it.
set -euo pipefail

cd "$(dirname "$0")"
[ -d together-city-react ] || { echo "!! Run this from the Together-Ai repo root."; exit 1; }

if [ -f .git/index.lock ] && [ ! -s .git/index.lock ]; then
  echo "== clearing a stale empty .git/index.lock"
  rm -f .git/index.lock
fi

NEEDS="The letter is printed on paper"
case "$(git log --oneline -40)" in
  *"$NEEDS"*) echo "== \"$NEEDS\" is already here. Nothing to do."; exit 0 ;;
esac

ALLOWED='^ M together-city-react/(public/assets/img/(apple-touch-icon-180|tc-icon-1024|tc-icon-192|tc-icon-512|tc-icon-maskable-512)\.png|public/downloads/TogetherCity\.apk)$'
DIRTY="$(git status --porcelain \
  | grep -Ev '^\?\? (land-.*\.sh|push-.*\.sh|.*\.patch)$' \
  | grep -Ev "$ALLOWED" || true)"
if [ -n "$DIRTY" ]; then
  echo "!! The tree carries changes this script did not expect:"; echo "$DIRTY"; exit 1
fi

PATCH="$(mktemp "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/land.XXXXXX")"
trap 'rm -f "$PATCH"' EXIT
cat <<'B64EOF' | tr -d '\n' | openssl base64 -d -A > "$PATCH"

B64EOF
WANT="871062867ec65223700ab44f4b9c74e38e4123fcd8ef6536ff9cecc535af5dfb"
GOT="$(shasum -a 256 "$PATCH" | awk '{print $1}')"
[ "$GOT" = "$WANT" ] || { echo "!! Patch is corrupt."; echo "   want $WANT"; echo "   got  $GOT"; exit 1; }
echo "== patch verified"
git apply --check -C1 "$PATCH" || { echo "!! Patch does not apply cleanly. Nothing written."; exit 1; }
git apply -C1 "$PATCH"
echo "== applied"

# THE PAPER. The owner's own scan, made seamless and flattened so tiling does
# not read as a grid, at 512px and 2.9 KB.
PAPER=together-city-react/public/assets/img/letter-paper.webp
cat <<'PAPEREOF' | tr -d '\n' | openssl base64 -d -A > "$PAPER"

PAPEREOF
PWANT="f4e9282c7d0da5f33748e0ba89692ab8605069e322773b66121bca9e63230f6e"
PGOT="$(shasum -a 256 "$PAPER" | awk '{print $1}')"
[ "$PGOT" = "$PWANT" ] || { echo "!! The paper is corrupt."; echo "   want $PWANT"; echo "   got  $PGOT"; exit 1; }
echo "== paper written ($(wc -c < "$PAPER") bytes)"

cd together-city-react
npx tsc --noEmit
npx vitest run
node scripts/a11y-audit.mjs
node scripts/motion-ceiling.mjs
node scripts/lint-ceiling.mjs
npx vite build
cd ..

git add together-city-react/src/styles/tokens.css \
        together-city-react/src/styles/layout.css \
        together-city-react/src/styles/relief.css \
        together-city-react/src/app/letter-surface.test.ts \
        together-city-react/src/app/relief.spec.ts \
        together-city-react/src/features/astrology/api.ts \
        together-city-react/src/features/astrology/components/Letter.tsx \
        together-city-react/src/features/astrology/pages/AstroToday.tsx \
        together-city-react/src/features/astrology/pages/AstroMonthly.tsx \
        together-city-react/public/assets/img/letter-paper.webp
git commit -F - <<'MSG'
The letter is printed on paper

The owner's brief was one sentence long underneath everything else in it: this
should feel like opening a letter, not like reading an article in a dashboard.
The backend already made it a letter — eighty to a hundred and fifty words, a
title, and a closing. This is the page it arrives on.

White paper, black type, a serif title, one column six hundred and forty pixels
wide, and no card around any of it. THE SIDEBAR IS UNTOUCHED — not restyled,
not resized, not lightened. That was the instruction and it is also the better
design: a dark rail against a lit page is the shape of a desk with a letter on
it, which is more interesting than either half alone.

--letter-paper IS NOT --paper, AND THAT IS THE WHOLE TRAP. `--paper` already
exists as a core token and five hubs re-point it — astrology points it at
#000000. The first attempt at this page used it, and the surface rendered pure
black no matter how hard the selector was scoped, because the token is DOING
ITS JOB: it is the city's ground and it changes with the room. A letter's paper
does not change with the room. So four tokens are declared at :root, re-pointed
by nothing, and the tint is sampled from the owner's own scan rather than
chosen, so the flat colour behind the texture is the texture's own average and
the join is invisible where the tile ends.

THE INK IS MEASURED. Title 15.2:1, body 10.5:1, label 5.6:1. The label began at
#8a857c, which is 3.0 — under the bar, on 11px uppercase, which is the smallest
and most easily missed text on the page.

THE PAPER IS THE OWNER'S OWN SCAN, MADE TILEABLE. A 512px tile mirrored about
its own centre so the edges match by construction, then flattened against a
28px blur so the large-scale drift in the photograph does not print as a quilt
of light and dark squares once it repeats. 2.9 KB, which is less than the
letter it sits under.

AND IT DOES NOT BLEED WITH A NEGATIVE MARGIN, BECAUSE THIS FILE ALREADY KNOWS
BETTER. The obvious way to make a surface reach the edges of the content column
is to cancel the shell's padding with `margin: -36px -44px`, and
letter-surface.test.ts exists because somebody did exactly that and it was
wrong within a day: the padding changes at 1100px and the margin did not, so
between two widths the surface sat notched away from its own column. That guard
caught this change too, before it shipped, and the sanctioned form — an
override on `.tc-shell .tc-main > .letter-page` that sets padding rather than
cancelling it — is correct at every width by construction.

The guard's anchor moved from `.letter-sky {` to `.letter-page {` with the
rename. Worth naming, because an anchor that matches nothing makes every
assertion in that file vacuous, and a file of tests that pass by not running is
worse than no file: the `expect(start).toBeGreaterThan(-1)` on the line below it
is the only thing standing between a rename and silence.

THE DISPLAY SERIF IS BORROWED, AND THE BORROWING IS NOW A RULE. relief.spec.ts
grants two typefaces to the nutrition press and says a new wearer needs its own
line and its own reason. `.letter-title` is a fourth wearer of the FACE ONLY —
not the mono, not the paper, not one press- class — because a letter has a
title, one line, set large, and this application owns exactly one display face
that can set one. The alternative was a fourth font file for two pages. So the
reason is written into the spec, and assertion 4 names the single selector
allowed to read `--press-serif` and fails on a second. It reads BOTH
stylesheets: the borrower is in layout.css, and the three assertions above it
read relief.css only, so a guard that stopped at the file boundary would have
had a door in it.

The drop cap goes with the card — it was what told you this was a letter when
the page could not. The astrology hub's one remaining rule in relief.css was
its letterpress correction for a dark ground, and the letter has its own ground
now, so that half of the rule leaves too.

`title` on the API type is OPTIONAL and the composition closes up around a
missing one. Letters written before titles existed are still in the archive and
still have to render; requiring one would break the past to display the present.

Rendered against the real cascade before this landed — the real stylesheets in
main.tsx order, the real Instrument Serif file, inside a real `.tc-shell` with
the real sidebar beside it — at 1440 and at 390.

tsc clean, vitest green, a11y 0, motion at ceiling, lint at ceiling, vite build
clean.

MSG
echo "== committed"

echo
echo "==============================================================="
echo " Landed: $NEEDS — push and Vercel ships it."
echo " /astrology/today and /astrology/monthly are paper now."
echo " The sidebar is exactly as it was."
echo "==============================================================="
